From 49d8f6871cf708e17804667a31c252a7a05223be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Durham <amdnative@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 17:18:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] hyundai: FCA11-long personality-indexed braking strength
 (relaxed 0.12 / standard 0.20 / aggressive 0.30 g)

The driver's LongitudinalPersonality (already the feel dial for the pedal launch ceiling / A_CRUISE_MAX / interceptor
cap via CarControlSP.personality) now owns the FCA11-long COMMANDED decel cap too:
- fca11_long.py: PERSONALITY_MAX_DEC tier table (relaxed 12 / standard 20 / aggressive 30 raw = 0.12/0.20/0.30 g);
  clamp_dec_cmd(dec_cmd, personality) and Fca11LongBrake.update(..., personality) index the cap; unknown -> standard.
  Standard's 20 is the new default (a bare call / sim / legacy caller gets the middle, never the strongest).
- gas_interceptor.py: create_gas_command threads its personality arg into fca11_brake.update.
- Every tier <= the panda gate HYUNDAI_FCA11_LONG_MAX_DEC (30, personality-agnostic): python-only, no safety change.
- Tests: test_fca11_long.py TestPersonalityStrength (per-tier cap + emitted frame + OFF-inert + fallback + gate
  invariant) and test_gas_interceptor.py wire-path; two pre-existing personality-independent pins updated.

No panda/opendbc safety files touched (firmware 00e086b9 valid); no resume/stop change; toggle-OFF byte-for-byte inert.
